<article class="env-corollary" id="FA620C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/FA620C">Corollary <span data-tag="FA620C">2.3.2.2</span> <span class="named">(Joyal <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/joyalnotpub">joyalnotpub</a>]</span>)</span>.</a> A simplicial set $\calC $ is an $\infty $-category if and only if the restriction map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Fun (\Delta ^2,\calC ) \rightarrow \Fun (\Lambda ^2_1, \calC ) \]
</div>
  <p> is a trivial fibration. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Proposition <a href="/tag/BE5D0B" data-tag="BE5D0B">2.3.2.1</a>, $\calC \rightarrow \ast $ is an inner fibration if and only if $S$ has the extension property with respect to each of the inclusions in the class $A_2$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>